<script setup lang="ts">import PageHeading from '@/components/PageHeading.vue'; import AppIcon from '@/components/AppIcon.vue'; import NoticeBox from '@/components/NoticeBox.vue'</script>
<template><div class="container narrow"><PageHeading back="/settings" eyebrow="A PRIVATE SPACE, BY DESIGN" title="Your home isn’t our data." subtitle="How this implementation handles scans, photos and permissions."/><section class="card detail-card prose"><div class="privacy-symbol"><AppIcon name="shield" :size="46"/></div><h2>Local work, deliberate sharing.</h2><p>Project records and assets are stored in IndexedDB in this browser or native WebView. Native scanners also keep private app-storage recovery snapshots until you save or discard them. Capture geometry is reconstructed on-device, without a reconstruction backend.</p><h3>What is not included</h3><p>This app has no advertising trackers, cloud account, analytics SDK, automatic upload, geolocation collection, face recognition or cloud anchors. It does not send a scan to the WiseStay backend or publish a listing. No remote sign-in or authorization is simulated.</p><h3>Camera access</h3><p>The camera is requested only for an explicit capture or selected photo action. Point the camera only at spaces you are allowed to record. Review models and exports for people, documents, valuables, entry codes and other sensitive details.</p><h3>Device protection and backups</h3><p>Local storage is not a separately encrypted application vault. People with access to your unlocked device or browser profile may be able to view your projects. Operating-system backups and policies can vary. Use device encryption and a screen lock. Clearing site data or uninstalling may remove your work.</p><h3>Exported files</h3><p>A W3D backup includes original scan geometry, photos, notes, room outlines and annotations. Non-destructive crops do not remove original geometry from a backup. GLB, PLY and OBJ exports use the current crop and transforms. Choose an encrypted W3D backup to protect file contents using AES-GCM and a passphrase-derived key. Passphrases are not stored and cannot be reset.</p><h3>Reference images</h3><p>Newly added reference photos are decoded and re-encoded locally to remove original EXIF metadata, including embedded location metadata. Sensitive information visible inside the image is not automatically redacted.</p><h3>Deleting a project</h3><p>Project deletion removes its local database assets and available recovery captures. It cannot delete files already exported, sent to another app, included in device backups or held by another person. Secure physical erasure from flash storage is not guaranteed by a web application.</p><h3>Browser installation and platform services</h3><p>The web app must first download its own files. Its service worker caches the application shell for later offline use; initial installation is not offline. Native AR platform components can have their own installation, update and diagnostic behaviour, separate from this application’s local reconstruction pipeline.</p><NoticeBox><strong>Android ARCore disclosure</strong>This application runs on Google Play Services for AR (ARCore), which is provided by Google LLC and governed by the Google Privacy Policy. Review Google’s policy before enabling the platform service.</NoticeBox><h3>Before public distribution</h3><p>This is an implementation-specific privacy description, not a substitute for the operator’s legally reviewed privacy notice. Before an app-store or production release, complete platform privacy declarations, licence review, device qualification and any jurisdiction-specific obligations.</p></section></div></template>
